{{TranslationNeeded}}
'''Fish Cat''' is one of the [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]]. He is available after clearing [[Madagascar (Empire of Cats)|Madagascar]] in ''Empire of Cats: Chapter 1'' for 6000 XP, or via the [[Cat Capsule]]. [[True Form]] added in [[Version 2.0 Update|Version 2.0]] doubles health and attack and grants a 2% chance to perform [[Critical Hit]]s, but has a longer recharge time.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 6
|rarity = N
|name1 = Fish Cat
|name2 = Whale Cat
|name3 = Island Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Whale Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Island Cat''' at level 20+10 using [[Normal Cat Capsule|Cat Tickets]].

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is great in [[Empire of Cats]] for clearing out [[Pigge]]s and [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]], and in [[Stories of Legend]] for [[St. Pigge the 2nd]]s but he loses use quickly due to high cost and low range. It is better to stack long ranged cats such as [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Gross Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Lizard Cat]].

However, Fish Cat still has his uses as a melee attacker. [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] is a major example because that enemy has high range and a slow attack rate, allowing him to destroy lots of ranged units quickly but not tanky melee units which could withstand him easily, and same goes for a few others like [[Kory]]/[[Master A.]]

==='''True Form'''===
Island Cat gains a big jump in strength, with increased health and high attack power, as well as a 2% chance to do [[Critical Hit]]s. He works well with his [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed counterpart]] against [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and, to a much lesser extent, [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies. However, in a normal situation, it is still better to avoid using this Cat against Metals due to his abysmally low (2%) critical chance.

Island Cat shines the most when you are able to stack long-ranged cats with protection from meatshields against non-metal enemies. Island Cat is also useful against [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave Attackers]], [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance enemies]] or simply those with great range, such as [[Kory]], [[Dolphina]] and [[Professor A.]], due to his high health. Of course, it goes without saying that a high level Island Cat is required, otherwise he does not have the necessary health to be worth his cost.

{{Job|Classification = Melee & Tanker}}

